# The system the root task starts at boot. One program per line:
#
#   name      process name (also how the console labels its output)
#   image     boot module holding its ELF executable
#   priority  1..250; no higher than the root task's
#   provides  service it serves on the endpoint in its slot 1, or -
#   uses      services it may call, comma-separated, or -; they land in
#             slots 2, 3, ... in this order, each with its own badge
#   devices   hardware it drives (com1, pci), or -; it gets a notification
#             in slot 8 and each device's capabilities from slot 9 on
#   quota     objects/pages it may create (a factory in slot 7), or -
#   arg       number passed to main()
#
# blk uses pci twice: two capabilities with different badges, which look
# like two separate clients to the PCI server (it checks that the second
# one can't take the device the first one claimed).
#
# name      image         priority  provides  uses              devices  quota  arg
console     console.elf   200       console   -                 com1     -      0
pci         pci.elf       180       pci       console           pci      16/0   0
blk         blk.elf       150       blk       console,pci,pci   -        4/8    0
hello       hello.elf     100       -         console           -        -      0
fs          fs.elf        140       fs        console,blk       -        -      0
cat         cat.elf       100       -         console,fs        -        -      0
